    "prompt": "Production asset: exactly NINE different isolated individual trees in a transparent3x3 equal-cell sprite atlas, row-major order. The supplied game building artwork is STYLE ONLY: match palette, camera, shading and painterly material treatment, but do not copy any reference subjects or ground patches.\nFixed orthographic2:1 dimetric game camera; ground axes at+26.565/-26.565 degrees, no perspective convergence. Northwest daylight, restrained warm hand-painted miniature style. Full crowns, trunks, roots and a tiny soft contact shadow are visible.\nShared physical scale with game buildings: one ground tile is16m square, an adult is1.75m and a door is2.1m. Do not draw people, doors or buildings. The normalized256px cell uses13.15px per vertical metre. Tree heights vary naturally; do not enlarge shorter species to fill their cells.\nEvery exposed trunk ROOT FOOT meets the shared horizontal baseline at95.5% of its cell height, centred horizontally. The baseline is the actual trunk foot, never the bottom of scenery. NO GRASS, SOIL, SNOW DISC, ROCKS, GROUND MOUND OR BASE PLATFORM; only the tree and a tiny contact shadow below its root. Crown and all branches stay inside their own cell with generous transparent gutters. Keep side gutters at least12% of cell width and top gutters at least10%. Tiny contact shadows fade out before the cell bottom. No long baked directional shadow; the game supplies the projected ground shadow.\nBroad asymmetrical foliage masses and clear species silhouettes readable at Region and Town zoom. A few large boughs and trunk forks; no individual leaves, fine needle lines, stippling, scratches, tiny bark fissures, tiny fruit dots, lettering or botanical labels. Each requested species has distinct branch architecture and crown proportions.\nGenuine transparent RGBA background; no coloured backdrop, checkerboard, ground rectangle, floating plinth, pots, frame, labels or UI. Exactly one whole tree per cell; no forest groups.\nCold northern woodland: cool sage and blue-green, pale bark, restrained ivory snow on upper branches and at roots. Keep tree anatomy visible.\nSlot 1: arctic-birch, 7m tall, 92.0px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Low many-stemmed silver trunk with a spreading rounded sage crown.\nSlot 2: mountain-birch, 10m tall, 131.5px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Bent pale trunks and a broad windswept yellow-green crown with light snow.\nSlot 3: silver-birch, 14m tall, 184.1px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Tall white trunk with a loose light silvery green crown and open lower branches.\nSlot 4: grey-alder, 11m tall, 144.6px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Compact cool green oval crown above several silver-grey trunks.\nSlot 5: green-alder, 8m tall, 105.2px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Low wide dark green lobed crown on visibly branching warm grey stems.\nSlot 6: balsam-poplar, 14m tall, 184.1px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Upright broad oval blue-green crown on a straight dark trunk.\nSlot 7: quaking-aspen, 13m tall, 170.9px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Slender pale trunk and a rounded muted golden crown with large leaf masses.\nSlot 8: feltleaf-willow, 8m tall, 105.2px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Low spreading silvery sage crown above an open forked cool brown trunk.\nSlot 9: goat-willow, 10m tall, 131.5px vertical tree height in the normalized256px cell. Broad rounded grey-green crown on a stout branching pale trunk, sparse snow.",
